  "raw_html": "<button type='button' role='link' class='btn btn-link p-0 text-start' id='link_16' aria-label=\" NOIDA Toll Bridge Company Ltd.  versus Federation of NOIDA Residents Welfare Association and Others pdf\"  class='noToken' href='#' onclick=javascript:open_pdf('16','2024','2024_12_1997_2042','2024INSC1027'); ><font size='4'> <strong>NOIDA TOLL BRIDGE COMPANY LTD. <span class='fst-italic'> versus </span>FEDERATION OF NOIDA RESIDENTS WELFARE ASSOCIATION AND OTHERS </strong>- <span class='escrText'>[2024] 12 S.C.R. 1997</span><span class='ncDisplay'>2024 INSC 1027</span><input type='hidden' id='cnr' value=ESCR010007902024></button></font><br><strong>Coram : SURYA KANT<sup style=\"color: #268e97;font-size: 22px;top: 0;\" class=\"tooltip-sup\" data-tooltip=\"Author\">*</sup>, UJJAL BHUYAN</strong><br> Issue for Consideration The issue concerned a challenge to collection and levying of toll, as legitimised by provisions enumerated in Agreement dated 12.11.1997 (Concession Agreement), executed between Appellant-NOIDA Toll Bridge Company Limited (NTBCL), the Development Authority (NOIDA) and the Infrastructure Leasing and Financial Services Limited (IL&amp;FS); The Concession Agreement conferred upon NTBCL the rights necessary for implementation of the Delhi NOIDA Bridge Project or the Delhi-NOIDA Direct Flyway (DND Flyway/Project) and, in<br><strong class='caseDetailsTD' ><span style='color:#212F3D' > Decision Date :</span><font color='green'> 19-12-2024</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Case No :</span><font color='green'>  No. 14826/2024</font>   <span style='color:#212F3D' > |  Bench :</span><font color='green'>  Judges</font></strong><div class='row my-1 mt-2 border bg-light'><div class='col-auto'><a href='#' class='btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm my-1' onclick=open_splitview('16','2024','2024_12_1997_2042','2024INSC1027','S')><i <i class='fas fa-columns me-2'></i>Split view</a></div><div class='col-auto'><a href='#' class='btn btn-outline-secondary btn